### Links and Anchors

The term **anchor** specifically refers to the `<a>` element's ability to mark a precise location in a webpage that can be jumped to, like bookmarking a spot within the same document. [MDN: Creating links](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Learn_web_development/Core/Structuring_content/Creating_links)

#### Nesting anchors

Which of these are valid HTML?

```html
<p>Here is a <a href="page.html">link</a> in text.</p>
<span class="inline"><a href="page.html">click here</a></span>
<a href="page.html"><span class="highlight">styled link</span></a>
<h1><a href="/home">Welcome to our page!</a></h1>
<a href="/index.html"><img src="pic.jpg" alt="image"></a>
```

<ExerciseCard question={getQuestion('nesting-anchors')} />

